# Pinned dependencies. Both are build inputs whose exact revision changes behaviour, so both
# are submodules: bumping ocgcore in particular can alter duel outcomes and invalidate stored
# replays (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md R5).
#
# The ProjectIgnis card script collection is deliberately NOT here. It is fetched by
# `make data-scripts` into data/base/script/, which is gitignored. Pinning it would mean a new
# card does not work until someone raises the pin by hand, and that contradicts Principle 2 of
# the project: new cards must work as soon as their Lua exists. The collection receives commits
# daily. Replays record its SHA instead of the build pinning it; see "Why the script collection
# is not a submodule" in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 7.
#
# Recommendation: leave it as it is until you have stored replays you care about. If replay
# fidelity across script updates turns into a real complaint rather than a theoretical one,
# switch then -- it is a ten-line change.

[submodule "native/godot-cpp"]
	path = native/godot-cpp
	url = https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp.git
	branch = 4.5
[submodule "native/vendor/ocgcore"]
	path = native/vendor/ocgcore
	url = https://github.com/edo9300/ygopro-core.git
